# The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and then `COPY . .`, so without this the host's
# node_modules is copied over the container's freshly installed one — including
# platform-specific binaries built for the developer's machine rather than the
# image.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: docs/ and *.md. HelpView globs
# `/docs/user-guide/**/*.md` at build time (HelpView.tsx:147) and compiles the
# guide into the bundle, so excluding either would produce an image whose in-app
# user guide is silently empty.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/

# Test and CI output — rebuilt or irrelevant to the image
test-results/
playwright-report/
e2e/
*.log

# Repository and process metadata — not read by the build
.git/
.github/
.specify/
.claude/
specs/
requirement-specs/
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
.env*
.DS_Store
